# Normalise line endings in the repository, not in the working tree.
#
# Why this matters here: the determinism gate (G5) re-runs the benchmark and
# compares the artifact with `git diff --exit-code`. With core.autocrlf=true on
# Windows, a file committed with LF is checked out with CRLF, so a regenerated
# file can differ purely by line ending while the numbers are identical. That
# turns a reproducibility check into a coin flip.
#
# input:  commit LF (canonical, so hashes and diffs are stable across platforms)
# output: LF in the working tree too, so "what you see is what was committed"
#       and regenerating a file produces no spurious diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched.
#
# One pattern per line on purpose. In a multi-pattern line only the LAST pattern
# may carry attributes, so "*.png *.jpg binary" silently leaves "*.jpg" invalid
# and git prints "*.jpg is not a valid attribute name" on every single command.
# Verbose, but it parses.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.h5 binary
*.onnx binary
*.joblib binary
*.pkl binary

# Generated artifacts are not committed, but keep the rule explicit.
results/** text eol=lf
repro/_logs/*.txt text eol=lf
repro/_logs/*.json text eol=lf
